    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the high-upside potential of **Junior Caminero** (75.43) and **Christian Yelich** (74.32), both of whom benefit significantly from a prime matchup against Imai and Kochanowicz. **Junior Caminero** is our strongest play, leveraging a massive +19% SP skill bonus and a favorable slot in the four-hole to maximize run production. Similarly, **Christian Yelich** receives a dual boost from a high-efficiency batting order spot and dynamic platoon splits, making him a cornerstone for our daily efficiency. Meanwhile, **Casey Schmitt** (63.20) provides an underrated profile for today; while his raw base is modest, his elite matchup against Gordon, T and a rare +2% bonus for a slow delivery\u2014which plays directly into our focus on stolen bases\u2014makes him a high-floor asset in an otherwise volatility-prone outfield.\n\nOur primary bench decision centered on **Chase Meidroth** (53.67), who nearly cracked the utility spot but ultimately lost out due to the sheer concentration of talent in today's active rotation. While **Chase Meidroth** offered solid SP skill indicators, the optimized model preferred the higher xwOBA ceilings of **Yordan Alvarez** and **Kyle Schwarber**, even against the daunting presence of Yamamoto. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Trea Turner** (52.46) and **Kyle Schwarber** (54.15); while both occupy favorable spots in the lineup, they are facing a legitimate elite arm in Yamamoto. Their scores are tethered to the wind conditions and order status, but we must be prepared for reduced output if Yamamoto manages to suppress base-runners. We continue to monitor the status of **Lars Nootbaar** and **Hyeseong Kim**, but for today, the focus remains on capitalizing on the current active roster's platoon advantages.",
